text:
Kerry Back (kerryback@gmail.com)



Excel finance and statistics functions that HyperFormula 2.7 lacks: IRR, XIRR, VDB, INTERCEPT, FORECAST, PERCENTILE, QUARTILE, RANK, KURT, and the bond functions PRICE, YIELD, DURATION, MDURATION, ACCRINT, ACCRINTM, the COUP* functions, DISC, INTRATE, RECEIVED, PRICEDISC, PRICEMAT, YIELDDISC and YIELDMAT. It also makes a bare TRUE and FALSE work.
Load it after Handsontable:
&lt;script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hyperformula@2.7.1/dist/hyperformula.full.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/handsontable@14.6.1/dist/handsontable.full.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://apps.kerryback.com/finance-functions.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
Then build the engine with the named expressions:
const hf = HyperFormula.buildEmpty({ licenseKey: 'internal-use-in-handsontable' },
                                   FinanceFunctions.namedExpressions);
The comment at the top of the file has the details.

